<title>GREECE: Greek Oct building materials price index up 7.5pct.</title>
<headline>Greek Oct building materials price index up 7.5pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's building materials price index for new housing rose 7.5 percent year-on-year in October against a 7.1-percent increase in September, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The index rose an average 7.2 percent year-on-year in the January-October 1996 period versus 7.0 percent and 6.0 percent in the same period in 1995 and 1994, respectively, it said.</p>
<p>					Oct 96   Sept 96   Oct 95</p>
<p>    Month/month change (pct)    0.4     2.2	 0.0</p>
<p>    Year-on-year(pct)	     7.5     7.1	 7.8</p>
<p>    Index (1990=100)	    189.7   189.0     176.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
